<resources>
    <!-- Refresh rate.  Without an override AOSP leaves config_defaultRefreshRate at
         60, which DisplayModeDirector turns into a global [0, 60] Hz render vote, so
         scrolling and animations run at 60 fps on the 144 Hz panel.  The panel
         overlay (overlay/FrameworksResCommon_Sys) clears that cap, and 120 is the
         default user peak, so the device starts at 120 Hz and 144 Hz stays
         selectable in Settings.  The panel modes are 30/60/90/120/144
         (ro.config.lgsi.default_refreshrate=120,
         ro.config.lgsi.surface_flinger.available_refreshrates=30_60_90_120_144). -->
    <integer name="config_defaultPeakRefreshRate">120</integer>

    <!-- Color modes (Settings > Display > Colors): Natural, Boosted, Adaptive.
         Adaptive (persist.sys.sf.native_mode=2, system_ext.prop) is the default.
         The vendor HAL also defines the render intents 256..265; they are not
         AOSP colour modes but raw values (SurfaceFlinger's Output.cpp passes them
         straight to the HWC as the render intent), so they are left out here. -->
    <integer-array name="config_availableColorModes">
        <item>0</item>
        <item>1</item>
        <item>3</item>
    </integer-array>

    <!-- Display white balance: the "Adapt color to environment" feature
         (Settings > Display, com.lenovo.settings.display.AutoColorPreferenceController,
         Settings.System "auto_color_temperature").

         The AOSP controller is used here: it reads
         auto_color_temperature from Settings.System and listens to the
         qti.sensor.rgb sensor - type 0x1fa2639 = 33171001, "tcs3408 RGB Sensor"
         (ams AG), values[0] = ambient colour temperature in Kelvin, values[1] =
         lux.  Readings are taken every 250 ms
         (config_displayWhiteBalanceColorTemperatureSensorRate) and smoothed by
         AmbientFilter.WeightedMovingAverageAmbientFilter: a time-weighted
         average over the last 10 s
         (config_displayWhiteBalanceColorTemperatureFilterHorizon), each sample
         weighted by its duration integrated over y = x + intercept
         (config_displayWhiteBalanceColorTemperatureFilterIntercept = 10.0).
         DisplayWhiteBalanceThrottler then drops updates that come too soon
         (5000 ms debounce for increases and decreases) or are too small (the
         base/increase/decrease threshold arrays).  The filtered ambient CCT
         maps to a display CCT through the linear spline of the two arrays
         below (ambient 2800..8500 -> display 5810..6710), and the low/high
         light bias splines blend that towards the fixed neutral CCT for
         filtered ambient lux below 50 / above 1000.  The result is applied as
         a per-panel diagonal gain matrix, animated over 2000 ms.

         Those bucket labels are NOT display colour temperatures.  On the TIANMA
         panel (/proc/cmdline:
         mdss_dsi_panel_lapis_tianma_nt36532_dsc_3k_video) the gain table is
         5800:(1.0,0.92,0.81) 6100:(1.0,0.92,0.84) 6500:(1.0,0.94,0.874)
         7100:(1.0,0.95,0.918) 7800:(1.0,0.97,0.966) 8500:(0.998,0.972,1.0)
         9500:(0.95,0.938,1.0): relative to its 7800 bucket the whole curve
         moves the white point only between ~5600 K and ~6700 K, leaving R at 1.0
         up to 7800 K and cutting G by <=5% and B by <=16%.  Feeding the labels to
         this controller as display CCTs (5800..9500) makes
         DisplayWhiteBalanceTintController adapt the white point to the real
         Planckian locus at 7800..9500 K, which with the AOSP sRGB primaries is
         R -7%..-15% and G -13%..-23% (peak-white normalised): a greenish, dimmer
         picture.

         Two more AOSP defaults are overridden here:
         - The AOSP nominal white is D65 coordinates
           (config_displayWhiteBalanceDisplayNominalWhiteCct=6500).  D65 is not on
           the Planckian locus, so "6500" already applied R +4.3% (a pink cast)
           whenever white balance was active.  The nominal white below is the
           6500 K point of ColorSpace.cctToXyz itself, so 6500 K - the CCT the
           neutral bucket uses - is an exact no-op matrix.
         - AOSP sets no config_displayWhiteBalance*Strong* tables, and
           DisplayPowerController enables strong mode for the idle brightness mode
           (DisplayPowerController.setDwbcStrongMode), where a null mapping means
           the raw ambient CCT is used.  The strong tables repeat the normal ones
           so idle mode cannot fall back to the raw sensor value.

         config_displayWhiteBalanceDisplayColorTemperatures fits the panel curve
         to this controller: for each bucket the AOSP matrix at the given CCT
         reproduces the bucket's G and B gains (relative to the untouched 7800
         bucket) within ~1.5%:
           ambient 2800 -> 5810 (R .931 G .936 B .841; panel rel. G .949 B .839)
           ambient 3500 -> 5934 (R .944 G .948 B .870; panel rel. G .949 B .870)
           ambient 4500 -> 6088 (R .959 G .962 B .906; panel rel. G .969 B .905)
           ambient 5500 -> 6281 (R .978 G .980 B .951; panel rel. G .979 B .950)
           ambient 6500 -> 6500 (no-op; the untouched 7800 bucket is
                                 (1.0, 0.97, 0.966), i.e. <=3.4% warmer)
           ambient 7500 -> 6500 (bucket 8500 wants B 1.035, above the peak-white
                                 normalisation, so it stays at no-op)
           ambient 8500 -> 6710 (R .974 G .972 B .998; panel rel. R .95 G .967)
         Worst case is the warmest point, relative luminance 0.928 - the same 7%
         as the 5800 bucket (0.929) - and the coolest is 0.974, so the panel is
         never yellow, red, green or noticeably dimmer.  The CCT clamp keeps the
         linear extrapolation of the spline inside the fitted range, and the
         250 ms sensor rate and throttler keep the AOSP defaults.

         No config_displayWhiteBalanceDisplayPrimaries override: AOSP falls back
         to its sRGB/D65 primaries (SurfaceFlinger has no panel identification
         data here, "screenPartStatus=UNSUPPORTED"), and the adaptation is
         relative so the primaries only scale the step sizes. -->
    <bool name="config_displayWhiteBalanceAvailable">true</bool>
    <!-- On by default -->
    <bool name="config_displayWhiteBalanceEnabledDefault">true</bool>
    <string name="config_displayWhiteBalanceColorTemperatureSensorName" translatable="false">qti.sensor.rgb</string>
    <integer name="config_displayWhiteBalanceColorTemperatureMin">5800</integer>
    <integer name="config_displayWhiteBalanceColorTemperatureMax">6750</integer>
    <!-- 6500 K Planckian white of ColorSpace.cctToXyz (x 0.31349, y 0.32366);
         with the AOSP config_displayWhiteBalanceDisplayNominalWhiteCct=6500 this
         makes 6500 K an identity matrix. -->
    <string-array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceDisplayNominalWhite">
        <item>0.968583</item>
        <item>1.000000</item>
        <item>1.121055</item>
    </string-array>
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceAmbientColorTemperatures">
        <item>2800.0</item>
        <item>3500.0</item>
        <item>4500.0</item>
        <item>5500.0</item>
        <item>6500.0</item>
        <item>7500.0</item>
        <item>8500.0</item>
    </array>
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceDisplayColorTemperatures">
        <item>5810.0</item>
        <item>5934.0</item>
        <item>6088.0</item>
        <item>6281.0</item>
        <item>6500.0</item>
        <item>6500.0</item>
        <item>6710.0</item>
    </array>
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceStrongAmbientColorTemperatures">
        <item>2800.0</item>
        <item>3500.0</item>
        <item>4500.0</item>
        <item>5500.0</item>
        <item>6500.0</item>
        <item>7500.0</item>
        <item>8500.0</item>
    </array>
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceStrongDisplayColorTemperatures">
        <item>5810.0</item>
        <item>5934.0</item>
        <item>6088.0</item>
        <item>6281.0</item>
        <item>6500.0</item>
        <item>6500.0</item>
        <item>6710.0</item>
    </array>
    <!-- Hold the neutral bucket below 50 lux (average of 10 samples) -->
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceLowLightAmbientBrightnesses">
        <item>40.0</item>
        <item>50.0</item>
    </array>
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceLowLightAmbientBiases">
        <item>0.0</item>
        <item>1.0</item>
    </array>
    <item name="config_displayWhiteBalanceLowLightAmbientColorTemperature" format="float" type="dimen">6088.0</item>
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceLowLightAmbientBrightnessesStrong">
        <item>40.0</item>
        <item>50.0</item>
    </array>
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceLowLightAmbientBiasesStrong">
        <item>0.0</item>
        <item>1.0</item>
    </array>
    <item name="config_displayWhiteBalanceLowLightAmbientColorTemperatureStrong" format="float" type="dimen">6088.0</item>
    <!-- Leave the panel untouched above 1000 lux -->
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceHighLightAmbientBrightnesses">
        <item>900.0</item>
        <item>1000.0</item>
    </array>
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceHighLightAmbientBiases">
        <item>0.0</item>
        <item>1.0</item>
    </array>
    <item name="config_displayWhiteBalanceHighLightAmbientColorTemperature" format="float" type="dimen">6500.0</item>
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceHighLightAmbientBrightnessesStrong">
        <item>900.0</item>
        <item>1000.0</item>
    </array>
    <array name="config_displayWhiteBalanceHighLightAmbientBiasesStrong">
        <item>0.0</item>
        <item>1.0</item>
    </array>
    <item name="config_displayWhiteBalanceHighLightAmbientColorTemperatureStrong" format="float" type="dimen">6500.0</item>
    <!-- Animate every colour temperature change over 2000 ms.  AOSP defaults
         to 1000 ms up and 40000 ms down, which would leave the panel warm for
         ~40 s after the light gets cooler. -->
    <integer name="config_displayWhiteBalanceTransitionTimeIncrease">2000</integer>
    <integer name="config_displayWhiteBalanceTransitionTimeDecrease">2000</integer>

    <!-- Double tap to wake (Settings > Display > Tap to wake).  The touch
         controller runs the gesture; the power HAL does not implement
         Mode.DOUBLE_TAP_TO_WAKE, so the device key handler applies the setting
         (keyhandler: DoubleTapToWake). -->
    <bool name="config_supportDoubleTapWake">true</bool>

    <!-- WiFi Display (Miracast) through the QTI session (WfdCommon) -->
    <bool name="config_enableWifiDisplay">true</bool>
</resources>
